Pokemon Emerald AI Move Probability Calculator - Project Plan
Goal
Build a tool that inputs current battle state and outputs move probabilities for the AI opponent. Must be fast enough for Monte Carlo simulations.

Architecture Decision
C backend + Web frontend

Extract battle logic from Emerald decomp (not using Showdown)
C backend for speed (microseconds per evaluation)
Simple web UI for state input and probability visualization
Optional: REST API if making it public
Step 1: Extract Battle Logic from Decomp
What to extract:
CalculateBaseDamage() and dependencies (~500 lines)
Type effectiveness tables (const arrays)
Battle struct definitions (BattleMon, Pokemon, etc.)
AI scoring functions from battle_ai_script_commands.c (few hundred lines)
Battle state tracking (status, volatile conditions, field effects)
Porting approach:
Remove GBA-specific macros (EWRAM_DATA, IWRAM_DATA - just delete them)
Convert globals to a BattleContext struct that gets passed around
Replace GBA types (u8 → uint8_t, etc.)
Replace RNG calls with standard C rand()
No assembly needed - battle logic is pure C
Output:
Standalone C library that can evaluate moves given a battle state, with no emulator required.

